ound\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"/><path d=\"M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1\"/></svg><svg class=\"qa-code-copy-icon-done\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"/></svg><span class=\"qa-code-copy-label-default\">Copy</span><span class=\"qa-code-copy-label-done\">Copied</span></button><pre class=\"qa-code-pre\"><code class=\"qa-code-block hljs\"><span class=\"hljs-title class_\">NaN</span> === <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">NaN</span>            <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// false</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-title class_\">NaN</span> == <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">NaN</span>             <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// false</span>\n[<span class=\"hljs-title class_\">NaN</span>].<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">includes</span>(<span class=\"hljs-title class_\">NaN</span>)    <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// true  — includes uses SameValueZero</span>\n[<span class=\"hljs-title class_\">NaN</span>].<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">indexOf</span>(<span class=\"hljs-title class_\">NaN</span>)     <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// -1    — indexOf uses ===</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Object</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">is</span>(<span class=\"hljs-title class_\">NaN</span>, <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">NaN</span>)    <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// true</span></code></pre></div><p>Checking it correctly:</p><div class=\"qa-code-wrap\"><span class=\"qa-code-lang\">javascript</span><button type=\"button\" class=\"qa-code-copy\" data-code=\"Number.isNaN(value)   // RIGHT — true only when value really is NaN\nisNaN(value)          // WRONG — coerces first, then checks\n\nisNaN('hello')        // true  &lt;- 'hello' is not NaN, it merely coerces to NaN\nNumber.isNaN('hello') // false &lt;- correct\" aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg class=\"qa-code-copy-icon-default\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"/><path d=\"M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1\"/></svg><svg class=\"qa-code-copy-icon-done\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"/></svg><span class=\"qa-code-copy-label-default\">Copy</span><span class=\"qa-code-copy-label-done\">Copied</span></button><pre class=\"qa-code-pre\"><code class=\"qa-code-block hljs\"><span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Number</span>.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">isNaN</span>(value)   <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// RIGHT — true only when value really is NaN</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">isNaN</span>(value)          <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// WRONG — coerces first, then checks</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">isNaN</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;hello&#x27;</span>)        <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// true  &lt;- &#x27;hello&#x27; is not NaN, it merely coerces to NaN</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Number</span>.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">isNaN</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;hello&#x27;</span>) <span class=\"hljs-comment\">// false &lt;- correct</span></code></pre></div><p class=\"qa-summary\"><strong>Note:</strong> <code>typeof NaN</code> returns <code>'number'</code>. NaN is still of type number, just an invalid value within it.</p><p class=\"qa-detail\"><strong>Takeaway:</strong> in real code <code>Number.isNaN()</code> is the only check to use; the global <code>isNaN()</code> is legacy and almost never matches the intent.</p>","references":[{"label":"MDN — NaN","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/NaN"},{"label":"MDN — Number.isNaN()","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Number/isNaN"}],"related":[{"url":"/q/201-su-khac-biet-giua-var-let-va-const-la-gi","title":"Sự khác biệt giữa var, let và const là gì?"},{"url":"/q/202-javascript-co-nhung-kieu-du-lieu-nguyen-thuy-primitive-types-nao","title":"JavaScript có những kiểu dữ liệu nguyên thuỷ (primitive types) nào?"},{"url":"/q/205-symbol-trong-javascript-la-gi-va-dung-de-lam-gi","title":"Symbol trong JavaScript là gì và dùng để làm gì?"},{"url":"/q/207-toan-tu-va-khac-nhau-nhu-the-nao","title":"Toán tử == và === khác nhau như thế nào?"},{"url":"/q/208-type-coercion-ep-kieu-tu-dong-trong-javascript-la-gi","title":"Type coercion (ép kiểu tự động) trong JavaScript là gì?"},{"url":"/q/209-truthy-va-falsy-values-trong-javascript-la-gi","title":"Truthy và falsy values trong JavaScript là gì?"},{"url":"/q/211-hoisting-trong-javascript-la-gi","title":"Hoisting trong JavaScript là gì?"},{"url":"/q/212-temporal-dead-zone-tdz-la-gi","title":"Temporal Dead Zone (TDZ) là gì?"}]}